(7426553, 1172799, 147247, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by posthumous:</b></div><hr/><i> the framing is strange and mysterious and creates multiple pictures.<br/> <br/>I''m hanging this in my fantasy art gallery<br/> <br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=1077279" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/50000-54999/50695/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1077279.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/50000-54999/50695/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1077279.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/50000-54999/50695/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1077279.jpg"/></a> </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thank you so much <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=50695" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Posthumous</a>! You made my day!</td>', 'Originally posted by posthumous: the framing is strange and mysterious and creates multiple pictures. I''m hanging this in my fantasy art gallery    Thank you so much  Posthumous! You made my day!', '2016-01-08 13:07:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(7426555, 1172042, 135027, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by blindjustice:</b></div><hr/><i> Beautifully painted sky and hill. I almost think there might be a more pleasing crop, but I could be wrong.<br/>Perhaps any perceived "imperfection" only makes it a better photograph, all the more left up to time and chance, and still realized successfully... </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I tried finding a better crop as well but preferred the original image! The ''imperfection'' bugs me but perhaps that is the beauty.. cheers!</td>', 'Originally posted by blindjustice: Beautifully painted sky and hill. I almost think there might be a more pleasing crop, but I could be wrong.Perhaps any perceived "imperfection" only makes it a better photograph, all the more left up to time and chance, and still realized successfully...   I tried finding a better crop as well but preferred the original image! The ''imperfection'' bugs me but perhaps that is the beauty.. cheers!', '2016-01-08 13:12:17.000000', NULL, 0),
